## Use

### The icon font

One class per icon, `{{ prefix }}-<name>`, on an empty element:

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="node_modules/{{ packageName }}/dist/web/{{ name }}.min.css" />

<i class="{{ prefix }}-{{ icon }}"></i>
```

With a bundler, `import '{{ packageName }}'` loads the same stylesheet and its font.

### The SVG sprite

One file for the whole set, and one `<use>` per icon:

```html
<svg width="{{ frame }}" height="{{ frame }}" fill="currentcolor" aria-hidden="true">
  <use href="node_modules/{{ packageName }}/dist/web/{{ name }}.svg#{{ icon }}"></use>
</svg>
```

### A single SVG file

```html
<img src="node_modules/{{ packageName }}/dist/svgs/{{ icon }}.svg" alt="" width="{{ frame }}" height="{{ frame }}" />
```

### Sass

The classes of the stylesheet, with the font served from a folder of your own, and the map of the icons for a selector of your own:

```scss
@use 'sass:map';
@use '{{ packageName }}/dist/web/{{ name }}.scss' as icons with (
  ${{ name }}-font-dir: '/fonts'
);

.my-icon::before {
  font-family: icons.${{ name }}-font;
  content: map.get(icons.${{ name }}-map, '{{ icon }}');
}
```

Sass finds the file in a load path that holds `node_modules`, and so does a bundler. With the package importer of Sass, `@use 'pkg:{{ packageName }}'` loads the same file.

{{# if ios }}
### iOS

Add `{{ ios.catalog }}` and `{{ ios.swiftFile }}` to the target of an app, from the archive `{{ name }}-ios-<version>.zip` of a release{{# if repository }} of [the repository]({{ repository }}){{/ if }}. Each icon is a case of `{{ ios.type }}`, and draws as a template image in the tint of its view:

```swift
Image({{ ios.type }}.{{ ios.case }})
UIImage({{ ios.type }}.{{ ios.case }})
```

{{/ if }}
{{# if android }}
### Android

Copy `res/` from the archive `{{ name }}-android-<version>.zip` of a release{{# if repository }} of [the repository]({{ repository }}){{/ if }} into `src/main/` of a module. Each icon is a drawable that takes the tint of its view:

```kotlin
Icon(painterResource(R.drawable.{{ android.drawable }}), contentDescription = null)
```

{{/ if }}
## The source

The package is built from the SVG files of {{# if repository }}its [repository]({{ repository }}){{ else }}`source/`{{/ if }} with [`@chassis-ui/icons`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@chassis-ui/icons). An icon is added or changed there, and never in the files of `dist/`.{{# if commands }} `{{ run }} build` writes the output into `dist/`, which is not committed, `{{ run }} lint` checks the files of the source, and `{{ run }} verify` checks that the source builds, that the registry of the code points and this README are up to date, and that no icon lost its code point.{{/ if }}{{# if preview }} `{{ run }} preview` writes the page of the set into `preview/` and serves it, to browse the icons, their classes, their code points and the code that draws them.{{/ if }}
